{%- comment -%}
  Hanken Grotesk, self-hosted.

  This used to be a render-blocking <link> to fonts.googleapis.com. That put a
  four-step chain in front of the first painted glyph — DNS + TLS to
  googleapis, 656B of CSS, DNS + TLS to gstatic, then the woff2 — on every cold
  load, and `display=swap` guaranteed a visible fallback-to-Hanken reflow at the
  end of it. theme-check flagged it three times (RemoteAsset).

  Google's css2 response was six @font-face blocks per subset all pointing at
  ONE file: Hanken Grotesk ships as a variable font, so a single woff2 covers
  400-900. Both subsets below are those exact files, served from Shopify's CDN.
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, which permits redistribution.

  Only latin is preloaded. latin-ext is declared with its unicode-range so the
  browser fetches it only if the page actually contains a character that needs
  it — preloading it would download 19KB for nothing on every English page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'hanken-grotesk-latin.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font' }}
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400 900;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ 'hanken-grotesk-latin.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400 900;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ 'hanken-grotesk-latin-ext.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0100-02BA, U+02BD-02C5, U+02C7-02CC, U+02CE-02D7, U+02DD-02FF, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+1D00-1DBF, U+1E00-1E9F, U+1EF2-1EFF, U+2020, U+20A0-20AB, U+20AD-20C0, U+2113, U+2C60-2C7F, U+A720-A7FF;
  }
  /* Metric-matched fallback (2026-09-21). font-display:swap paints the first
     frame in the fallback, and system-ui is ~6-9% narrower than Hanken at
     400-500, so text reflowed when the woff2 landed: the 390px hero subtitle
     went 4 lines -> 3 and its CTAs jumped 12px (CLS 0.014; 0.002-0.004 wider).
     These faces reshape local Arial to Hanken's box. Widths measured in Chrome
     (Hanken/Arial = 1.005-1.013 at 400-500; 0.942-0.957 at 600-900 against
     Arial Bold); vertical metrics from the shipped woff2 (UPM 1000, ascent 1000,
     descent 303, line gap 0), each override divided by size-adjust. The two
     weight ranges do not overlap, so nothing is synthetically bolded. No Arial
     (Android) = local() fails and the stack falls through to system-ui as before.
     Every stack that names Hanken must carry this family second: cartel.css
     (x2, !important), cartel-home.css .cl, cartel-conversion.css, gift_card. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk Fallback';
    src: local('Arial'), local('ArialMT');
    font-weight: 100 599;
    font-display: swap;
    size-adjust: 101%;
    ascent-override: 99%;
    descent-override: 30%;
    line-gap-override: 0%;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk Fallback';
    src: local('Arial Bold'), local('Arial-BoldMT');
    font-weight: 600 1000;
    font-display: swap;
    size-adjust: 95%;
    ascent-override: 105.3%;
    descent-override: 31.9%;
    line-gap-override: 0%;
  }
  :root{
    --font-body-family:'Hanken Grotesk','Hanken Grotesk Fallback',system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;
    --font-heading-family:'Hanken Grotesk','Hanken Grotesk Fallback',system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;
    --font-body-style:normal;--font-body-weight:400;--font-body-weight-bold:700;
    --font-heading-style:normal;--font-heading-weight:800;
  }
</style>
